                <pb facs="1215" n="929" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg929"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/1574</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4244. Department’s telegram 3036, March 14.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1230-f1"/>
                    Foreign Office informs me that French Government does not see its way to permit
                    the landing of supplies for Jewish hospitals at Jerusalem owing to their
                    objection to any modification of blockade of Syrian coast. British Government
                    shares the view expressed by French Government and to its great regret is
                    accordingly unable to agree to this humanitarian proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
